index 4479b53..5c7665e 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,31 @@
 
 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
+## Account settings and passkeys
+
+Signed-in readers can manage passkeys at `/devtools-times/account/settings`. The existing password login service authenticates readers; Astro keeps the resulting reader identity in an HttpOnly, SameSite session cookie. Successful sign-in opens settings, and the header exposes account settings and sign-out links.
+
+The settings panel lists provider details, registration and last-used dates, and allows readers to rename or remove their own keys. Removal returns the complete remaining credential list and shares it with the browser through the WebAuthn Signal API, including when the last key is removed. Unsupported browsers keep all management controls and explain how to remove stale keys in the password manager. Passkey nicknames are account-side labels, so renaming one does not send an account-profile rename signal.
+
+Because the existing external service has no credential-management API, this app owns the passkeys registered here. Existing credentials from other services are not fabricated or imported. Settings can register discoverable passkeys, including security keys, and the sign-in form can authenticate them. Registration and sign-in responses are verified by `@simplewebauthn/server` using session-bound, expiring challenges and required user verification. Username/password sign-in remains available after removing all passkeys.
+
+Use Node.js 24 or newer. Configure these server environment variables before deployment:
+
+| Variable | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN` | `https://astro-news-pytrpecapa-uc.a.run.app` | Exact trusted HTTPS origin used for WebAuthn verification. |
+| `WEBAUTHN_RP_ID` | Hostname from `WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN` | Stable relying-party ID used at registration, verification, and browser synchronization. |
+| `ACCOUNT_DB_PATH` | `./.data/accounts.sqlite` | SQLite credential and reader database. |
+| `SESSION_DIR` | `./.data/sessions` | Astro session storage directory. |
+
+For localhost development, set `WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN=http://localhost:4321` and `WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=localhost` (adjust the port to match your environment). The site base path is `/devtools-times/` and is not part of the WebAuthn origin. The browser always receives the RP ID from the server.
+
+Persist both database and session directories on durable storage. This storage configuration targets a single Node deployment; use a shared database and shared session driver before running multiple replicas. Changing the RP ID or losing the database makes previously registered keys unusable. Reader IDs are stable hashes of the exact username authenticated by the existing service; a service migration should preserve that identity mapping.
+
+Provider metadata is a trimmed local snapshot of the [passkey-authenticator-aaguids registry](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids), with compact icons for common providers. Unknown and zero AAGUIDs use a generic key icon. Provider metadata is only a visual hint and never controls authentication.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for the account endpoint and synchronization tests, and `pnpm build` for the production build. Tests invoke isolated route handlers and use a temporary database; they do not launch a server or import the generated server entrypoint.
+
 
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
